 "text": "In 1943, British spies fooled Hitler with a dead man. They dressed a body as a Royal Marines officer, Major William Martin. In his briefcase, fake secret letters saying the Allies would invade Greece, not Sicily. In his pockets, love letters, a photo of his fiancée, theatre tickets. They let him wash up in Spain. The Germans got copies. Hitler sent troops to Greece. Here's the trick. The small details made the big lie believable. It was called Operation Mincemeat. Follow for more dark psychology.",
